messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: python/libxml.c
Line: 465
Function: xmlOutputBufferCreatePythonFile
Bug type: use-after-free
CWE: CWE-416
Explanation: The function passes a PyObject* (file) as the I/O context to xmlOutputBufferCreateIO without increasing its reference count. The corresponding close callback (xmlPythonFileClose) also does not DECREF the object. This means the libxml2 output buffer holds a raw, non-owned pointer to the Python object. If the Python code drops its last reference to the file object while the output buffer still exists, subsequent callbacks (write/close) will operate on a freed PyObject, leading to a use-after-free.

Source context:
